// EXPECTED TO FAIL: a recursive block whose CLAUSES rename the declared parameters.
//
// THIS IS A SOUNDNESS GATE, not style. `f(j, ZERO)` against declared params `(i, k)` makes
// slot 0 read as a closed PATTERN -- the names differ, and the parser cannot tell a renamed
// variable from a constant, both being lower-case single tokens absent from the param list.
// So the generator emits a base branch `i = j`, which the obligation restates at the
// parameters as `j = j`. That is TRUE, so the disjunct fires unconditionally, the generated
// predicate holds everywhere, and the termination obligation is dischargeable by
// `[by reflexivity]` plus `tautology` with NO INDUCTION AT ALL -- verified before the fix.
//
// That is the vacuous discharge design/definition-wellformedness.md's soundness argument had searched
// for and not found, so the agreement the generator depends on is now enforced rather than
// assumed. Four `std` declarations carried the mismatch; all are fixed.
sort N
const Z: N
oper prev(n: N) => N requires n != Z
oper add(a: N, b: N) => N

oper f(i: N, k: N) => N:
  f(j, Z) = j;
  f(j, m) = add(j, f(j, prev(m))) when m != Z.
  termination(peano): _, {fIsGrounded, fGrounded}
